{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-4f48f247-4c51-4673-86e6-b1aa5404303e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-88d38b5a0a06e151","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8007-ld5kqog6/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8007-decomposition.md","content":"# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8007\n\nFeature Store Admin UI — Self-Service Instance Deployment and Management\n\n## Triage\n\nNot below-threshold: although the code change concentrates in odh-dashboard, the strategy spans\nmultiple distinct work streams (React frontend pages, RBAC/kustomize manifests, UXD design\nauthoring, cross-team validation, admin-guide documentation) and contains genuine unknowns\n(open questions on form field curation and backend-combination restrictions) whose answers\nchange what the create-form epic does. Not docs-only: odh-dashboard requires code changes.\n\nStaff Engineer Input section contains only template placeholder text — no overrides to apply.\n\n## Component Mapping\n\nCanonical component names from `.context/rhai-components.txt`:\n\n| Strategy component | Canonical component | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| odh-dashboard (frontend / backend / manifests) | AI Core Dashboard | Closest canonical name for the RHOAI dashboard; all three strategy rows map here |\n| feast-operator | Feature Store | No code changes expected — passive component validated by a different team |\n| UXD design assets | UXD | |\n| QE test suites | QE | |\n| Admin guides | Documentation | |\n\nBoth odh-dashboard and feast exist in `.context/architecture-context/` (odh-dashboard.md,\nfeast.md, feast-module-operator.md) — no new-component onboarding chain is needed.\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| RHAISTRAT-8007-E001 | Determine FeatureStore CRD field exposure and form constraints for TP create form | Investigation | Feature Store Engineering | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8007-E002 | UXD wireframes and interaction patterns for Feature Store admin UI | Implementation | UXD Team | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8007-E003 | Extend dashboard RBAC and feature flag for Feature Store admin operations | Implementation | Dashboard/Frontend Engineering | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8007-E004 | Feature Store instance create form wizard | Implementation | Dashboard/Frontend Engineering | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8007-E005 | Feature Store management list, detail, and delete pages | Implementation | Dashboard/Frontend Engineering | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8007-E006 | Feast operator validation for dashboard-created FeatureStore CRs | Implementation | Feature Store Engineering | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8007-E007 | QE validation of Feature Store admin UI (CRUD, RBAC tiers, disconnected) | Implementation | QE Team | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8007-E008 | Document Feature Store admin UI workflow in RHOAI admin guide | Implementation | Documentation Team | P1 |\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[RHAISTRAT-8007-E001 Investigation: CRD field set]\n    E002[RHAISTRAT-8007-E002 UXD designs]\n    E003[RHAISTRAT-8007-E003 RBAC + feature flag]\n    E006[RHAISTRAT-8007-E006 Feast operator validation]\n    E004[RHAISTRAT-8007-E004 Create form wizard]\n    E005[RHAISTRAT-8007-E005 List/detail/delete pages]\n    E007[RHAISTRAT-8007-E007 QE validation]\n    E008[RHAISTRAT-8007-E008 Admin guide docs]\n    E001 --> E004\n    E002 --> E004\n    E002 --> E005\n    E003 --> E007\n    E004 --> E007\n    E005 --> E007\n    E006 --> E007\n    E002 --> E008\n    E003 --> E008\n    E004 --> E008\n    E005 --> E008\n    E006 --> E008\n    E007 --> E008\n```\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| E001 → E004 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | The field-curation decision (all CRD fields vs curated subset, restricted backend combinations) rewrites the create-form wizard's scope. True gate with `rewrite` impact; wizard carries `gated_by`. |\n| E002 → E004 | Rule 12/13 (artifact consumer serial) | The wizard frontend builds against the UXD wireframes/interaction patterns; design is a build-against artifact, not configuration. |\n| E002 → E005 | Rule 12/13 | List/detail/delete pages likewise build against the UXD designs for the management page. |\n| E003 → E007 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | QE validates the RBAC extension (admin vs viewer enforcement) only after it is implemented. |\n| E004 → E007, E005 → E007 | Rule 12 | QE validates the built UI flows; validation work consumes completed implementations. |\n| E006 → E007 | Rule 12 | QE delete-flow/cleanup validation builds on the Feature Store engineering confirmation of operator reconciliation and resource cleanup. |\n| E002..E007 → E008 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring always last) | Docs describe what was built; blocked by all Implementation epics. These edges do not trigger priority inheritance (docs-authoring priority derived from strategy `priority: Major` → P1). |\n| E003 ∥ E004/E005 (no edge) | Rule 15 | Same repo, different areas (manifests/RBAC vs React frontend) → parallel; merge coordination, not dependency. RBAC correctness is enforced as an acceptance-criterion gate on the frontend and QE epics, not a DAG edge. |\n| E006 ∥ E004 (no edge) | Rule 13 (exclusion) | The FeatureStore CRD already exists; the validation epic produces a confirmation/report, not an artifact the wizard code builds against. Its outcome is a risk-reduction input handled as ACs (validate form fields against CRD OpenAPI schema), not a blocking edge. |\n| E001 ∥ E002 (no edge) | Rule 14 | Independent inputs (product/CRD decision vs design work); both gate the wizard in parallel. |\n\n## Investigation Analysis\n\nUnknowns scanned from the open questions table, risks, and assumptions:\n\n- **Form field curation + backend-combination restrictions (open questions 2 and 5)** — combined\n  into E001: both are resolved by the same analysis (CRD schema review producing a field-set and