{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9f26b321-a9c4-4fae-829e-817ffd85b58e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8da80f68a4dae41b","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8007-ld5kqog6/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8007-E003.md","content":"# Extend dashboard RBAC and feature flag for Feature Store admin operations\n\n## Description\n\nExtend the odh-dashboard's Kubernetes RBAC and feature-flag configuration so that platform\nadministrators can create, update, patch, and delete `FeatureStore` custom resources\n(feast.dev/v1) through the dashboard's existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through proxy, and so the\nnew admin UI can be progressively rolled out behind an `OdhDashboardConfig` feature flag.\nNo new backend routes are required: CRUD flows through the existing K8s API pass-through and\nreads through the existing `/api/featurestores` proxy.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Update the dashboard's ClusterRole manifest\n  (`manifests/core-bases/base/sa-rbac/cluster-role.yaml`) to add `create, update, patch,\n  delete` verbs for `feast.dev/featurestores`, using the feast-operator's\n  `featurestore-editor-role` as the reference for the minimum permission set.\n- Add/confirm the feature flag default in `OdhDashboardConfig` that gates the Feature Store\n  admin UI, so clusters without the Feast component enabled see no UI changes.\n- Verify viewer-tier permissions remain read-only via the existing\n  `featurestore-viewer-role` (get, list, watch on featurestores and featurestores/status) —\n  no escalation of non-admin permissions.\n- Confirm platform administrators hold sufficient RBAC to create `FeatureStore` CRs in\n  target namespaces with the extended ClusterRole (a strategy assumption marked\n  \"needs validation\").\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The dashboard ClusterRole grants `create, update, patch, delete` on\n  `feast.dev/featurestores`, and no broader permissions than the minimum set referenced from\n  the feast-operator editor role.\n- An admin user's forwarded token can create and delete a `FeatureStore` CR through the\n  dashboard's `/api/k8s/*` pass-through on a live cluster.\n- A non-admin (viewer) user's token is refused for write operations on\n  `feast.dev/featurestores` by the K8s API (RBAC enforced at the API level, not only in the\n  UI).\n- The Feature Store admin UI is gated behind an `OdhDashboardConfig` feature flag, defaulting\n  to off for clusters without the Feast component enabled.\n- RBAC changes are manifest-only; no new Go BFF module is introduced (FIPS posture unchanged).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Enables the P0 HLRs for admin deploy and delete of FeatureStore instances and the P1 HLR\n  for viewer read-only access (K8s-level enforcement), by providing the permission layer\n  those operations require. Does not itself deliver an HLR.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":42504,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98b7402301a08c80","agent_id":"a1cc435330cc27217","session_id":"ca7cb4a8-97e2-442a-8df6-df0a1f4664f3","uuid":"ae3886fb-0f17-4a7a-8180-984d7c3e1dd3","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:14:32.637Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8007"}
