{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-06ebe483-f64a-4171-9c7e-b590368b9af8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b43592eb0b9079b4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8007-ld5kqog6/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8007-E005.md","content":"# Feature Store management list, detail, and delete pages\n\n## Description\n\nBuild the Feature Store management surface in the odh-dashboard frontend: a list page\nshowing all `FeatureStore` instances across namespaces accessible to the user, a read-only\ndetail/inspect view of any instance, admin-initiated delete with a confirmation dialog, and\nreal-time deployment status tracking. Non-admin (viewer) users can browse instances but see\nno write controls.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Management list page: all `FeatureStore` CRs across the user's accessible namespaces, each\n  row showing name, namespace, deployment status (from `.status.conditions`), and creation\n  timestamp, with inspect and delete actions.\n- Status tracking: list/detail status reflects real-time readiness using the dashboard's\n  existing K8s watch/list patterns (no manual refresh), updating from \"Deploying\" to \"Ready\"\n  as conditions are met.\n- Read-only detail/inspect view: full `FeatureStore` CR spec (configured backends, registry\n  type, authorization mode, scaling settings, TLS status, materialization schedule) and\n  current status conditions, rendered without truncation; links to the Feast UI Route when\n  available for browsing feature metadata.\n- Delete flow: confirmation dialog, then `DELETE` of the `FeatureStore` CR via the existing\n  `/api/k8s/*` pass-through; the feast-operator's finalizers handle cleanup of owned\n  resources.\n- Viewer gating: non-admin users see list and detail views but no create or delete controls\n  (admin status check per existing dashboard patterns); write enforcement remains at the K8s\n  API via the user's token.\n- Feature-flag gating consistent with the `OdhDashboardConfig` flag.\n- Air-gapped support: no external network fetches in list/detail/delete rendering.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given FeatureStore instances exist in namespaces the admin can access, the management page\n  lists all of them with name, namespace, status, and creation timestamp, matching\n  `kubectl get featurestores -A` for those namespaces.\n- After instance creation, the list shows a \"Deploying\"-equivalent status that transitions\n  to \"Ready\" when conditions are met, updating within the dashboard's watch/poll cycle\n  without manual refresh.\n- Clicking an instance shows the full CRD spec and status conditions in a read-only view,\n  with all spec fields rendered without truncation.\n- Delete with confirmation removes the `FeatureStore` CR via the K8s API; the instance\n  disappears from the list and `kubectl get featurestore <name> -n <ns>` returns NotFound,\n  with the operator cleaning up owned Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, CronJobs, HPAs,\n  PDBs, and Routes.\n- A non-admin (viewer) user sees list and detail views but no create or delete controls.\n- Pages function without external network access.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- P0: view all FeatureStore instances with name, namespace, status, creation time.\n- P0: inspect the configuration of any instance in a read-only detail view.\n- P0: delete a FeatureStore instance with a confirmation dialog.\n- P0: deployment progress / readiness status visible in real time.\n- P1 (shared): non-admin viewers browse but cannot create/delete; disconnected/air-gapped\n  functioning.\n\nDepends on: the UXD wireframes/interaction patterns for the management page. The RBAC /\nfeature-flag configuration changes run in parallel; correct viewer and admin behavior is\nverified by this epic's acceptance criteria rather than a work dependency.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_to