(Investigation gates downstream) | The field-curation decision (all CRD fields vs curated subset, restricted backend combinations) rewrites the create-form wizard's scope. True gate with `rewrite` impact; wizard carries `gated_by`. |\n84\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 12/13 (artifact consumer serial) | The wizard frontend builds against the UXD wireframes/interaction patterns; design is a build-against artifact, not configuration. |\n85\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 12/13 | List/detail/delete pages likewise build against the UXD designs for the management page. |\n86\t| E003 → E007 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | QE validates the RBAC extension (admin vs viewer enforcement) only after it is implemented. |\n87\t| E004 → E007, E005 → E007 | Rule 12 | QE validates the built UI flows; validation work consumes completed implementations. |\n88\t| E006 → E007 | Rule 12 | QE delete-flow/cleanup validation builds on the Feature Store engineering confirmation of operator reconciliation and resource cleanup. |\n89\t| E002..E007 → E008 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring always last) | Docs describe what was built; blocked by all Implementation epics. These edges do not trigger priority inheritance (docs-authoring priority derived from strategy `priority: Major` → P1). |\n90\t| E003 ∥ E004/E005 (no edge) | Rule 15 | Same repo, different areas (manifests/RBAC vs React frontend) → parallel; merge coordination, not dependency. RBAC correctness is enforced as an acceptance-criterion gate on the frontend and QE epics, not a DAG edge. |\n91\t| E006 ∥ E004 (no edge) | Rule 13 (exclusion) | The FeatureStore CRD already exists; the validation epic produces a confirmation/report, not an artifact the wizard code builds against. Its outcome is a risk-reduction input handled as ACs (validate form fields against CRD OpenAPI schema), not a blocking edge. |\n92\t| E001 ∥ E002 (no edge) | Rule 14 | Independent inputs (product/CRD decision vs design work); both gate the wizard in parallel. |\n93\t\n94\t## Investigation