is covered by the RBAC extension epic's acceptance\n119\t  criteria.\n120\t\n121\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n122\t\n123\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n124\t|---|---|---|\n125\t| Deploy new FeatureStore via guided form wizard | P0 | E004 (enabled by E001, E002, E003) |\n126\t| View all FeatureStore instances with name/namespace/status/creation time | P0 | E005 (enabled by E002) |\n127\t| Inspect configuration in read-only detail view | P0 | E005 |\n128\t| Delete instance with confirmation dialog | P0 | E005 |\n129\t| Deployment progress / readiness status visible in real time | P0 | E005 |\n130\t| Non-admin viewers browse but cannot create/delete | P1 | E005 (UI gating), E003 (RBAC enforcement), validated in E007 |\n131\t| Admin UI functions in disconnected/air-gapped environments | P1 | E004 (bundled form assets), E007 (air-gapped validation) |\n132\t| Inline form validation guidance for CRD constraints | P2 | E004 (incidental to the wizard — shares the same form surface and validation logic; kept bundled per Step 4) |\n133\t\n134\tAll HLRs covered; no orphans. P2 inline validation is bundled into E004 rather than split: it is\n135\tUX polish falling out of the same form implementation (shared UI surface and validation rules),\n136\tnot a deferrable independent feature.\n137\t\n138\t## Health Warnings\n139\t\n140\t- **Internal contradiction — edit capability**: the open-questions table asks whether editing\n141\t  deployed instances should be supported, while Out-of-Scope explicitly defers it. Decomposition\n142\t  follows Out-of-Scope (no edit epic). Verify with PM if the open question is still live.\n143\t- **P1 epic validating P0 assumptions**: E006 (Feast operator validation) confirms the CRD\n144\t  stability assumption that the P0 wizard depends on, yet runs in parallel rather than blocking.\n145\t  This mirrors the strategy's own risk table (pin to feast.dev/v1, validate form fields against\n146\t  the CRD OpenAPI schema at build time). If CRD instability is