{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a94fbf5cada65c5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n3\ttitle: Determine FeatureStore CRD field exposure and form constraints for TP create\n4\t  form\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n6\tcomponent: Feature Store\n7\tteam: Feature Store Engineering\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tinvestigation_signals:\n12\t  question_specificity: 1\n13\t  source_accessibility: 1\n14\t  local_runnability: 0\n15\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n16\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n17\timplementation_type: null\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 0\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Determine FeatureStore CRD field exposure and form constraints for TP create form\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tResolve the open product/engineering question of what the Feature Store admin UI create form\n31\tshould expose for the Technology Preview: whether the form covers the full `FeatureStore` CRD\n32\tspec (feast.dev/v1) or a curated subset, and which store backend combinations should be\n33\trestricted or flagged (e.g., SQLite being development-only and unsuitable for production).\n34\tThe deliverable is a decided, written field-set and validation-constraint specification that\n35\tthe guided create form implementation builds against.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Review the `FeatureStore` CRD (feast.dev/v1) OpenAPI schema: registry type, online store\n40\t  backends (Redis, PostgreSQL, DynamoDB, SQLite), offline store backend, authorization mode\n41\t  (OIDC vs Kubernetes RBAC), TLS settings, scaling configuration, and materialization\n42\t  scheduling.\n43\t- Decide, with product management, the curated set of fields the TP form exposes versus\n44\t  advanced/optional fields, balancing admin usability against production-deployment adequacy.\n45\t- Decide which backend combinations are permitted, restricted, or warned against in the form\n46\t  for production readiness.\n47\t- Produce a field-set and validation-constraint specification (required fields, valid\n48\t  combinations, defaults, scaling prerequisites) suitable for driving form implementation\n49\t  and inline validation rules.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- A written specification exists listing every `FeatureStore` CRD field with a disposition:\n54\t  exposed in the TP form, omitted, or advanced-only — with rationale.\n55\t- Backend-combination restrictions are enumerated (which combinations are blocked, which\n56\t  produce warnings, and why), with development-only configurations identified.\n57\t- Product management and Feature Store engineering have signed off on the field set.\n58\t- The specification is sufficient for a form implementer to build the wizard and its inline\n59\t  validation without further schema decisions.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- Enables the P0 HLR \"deploy a new FeatureStore instance via a guided form wizard\" and the\n64\t  P2 HLR \"inline form validation guidance for CRD schema constraints\" by determining their\n65\t  scope. Does not itself deliver an HLR.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87a86ab7efa4cc07","agent_id":"aba39eb4d9d2cfbec","session_id":"ca7cb4a8-97e2-442a-8df6-df0a1f4664f3","uuid":"b54f2a0c-6885-4284-a5d8-fa26efae62b0","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:18:27.911Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a94fbf5cada65c5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
