{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8008fe18ef0352cc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E003\n3\ttitle: Extend dashboard RBAC and feature flag for Feature Store admin operations\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Extend dashboard RBAC and feature flag for Feature Store admin operations\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tExtend the odh-dashboard's Kubernetes RBAC and feature-flag configuration so that platform\n34\tadministrators can create, update, patch, and delete `FeatureStore` custom resources\n35\t(feast.dev/v1) through the dashboard's existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through proxy, and so the\n36\tnew admin UI can be progressively rolled out behind an `OdhDashboardConfig` feature flag.\n37\tNo new backend routes are required: CRUD flows through the existing K8s API pass-through and\n38\treads through the existing `/api/featurestores` proxy.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Update the dashboard's ClusterRole manifest\n43\t  (`manifests/core-bases/base/sa-rbac/cluster-role.yaml`) to add `create, update, patch,\n44\t  delete` verbs for `feast.dev/featurestores`, using the feast-operator's\n45\t  `featurestore-editor-role` as the reference for the minimum permission set.\n46\t- Add/confirm the feature flag default in `OdhDashboardConfig` that gates the Feature Store\n47\t  admin UI, so clusters without the Feast component enabled see no UI changes.\n48\t- Verify viewer-tier permissions remain read-only via the existing\n49\t  `featurestore-viewer-role` (get, list, watch on featurestores and featurestores/status) —\n50\t  no escalation of non-admin permissions.\n51\t- Confirm platform administrators hold sufficient RBAC to create `FeatureStore` CRs in\n52\t  target namespaces with the extended ClusterRole (a strategy assumption marked\n53\t  \"needs validation\").\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- The dashboard ClusterRole grants `create, update, patch, delete` on\n58\t  `feast.dev/featurestores`, and no broader permissions than the minimum set referenced from\n59\t  the feast-operator editor role.\n60\t- An admin user's forwarded token can create and delete a `FeatureStore` CR through the\n61\t  dashboard's `/api/k8s/*` pass-through on a live cluster.\n62\t- A non-admin (viewer) user's token is refused for write operations on\n63\t  `feast.dev/featurestores` by the K8s API (RBAC enforced at the API level, not only in the\n64\t  UI).\n65\t- The Feature Store admin UI is gated behind an `OdhDashboardConfig` feature flag, defaulting\n66\t  to off for clusters without the Feast component enabled.\n67\t- RBAC changes are manifest-only; no new Go BFF module is introduced (FIPS posture unchanged).\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- Enables the P0 HLRs for admin deploy and delete of FeatureStore instances and the P1 HLR\n72\t  for viewer read-only access (K8s-level enforcement), by providing the permission layer\n73\t  those operations require. Does not itself deliver an HLR.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87a86ab7efa4cc07","agent_id":"aba39eb4d9d2cfbec","session_id":"ca7cb4a8-97e2-442a-8df6-df0a1f4664f3","uuid":"c38ef133-4732-44aa-89e5-2d62f0833c26","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:18:29.775Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8008fe18ef0352cc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
