{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-824c53817a3db0ae","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E004\n3\ttitle: Feature Store instance create form wizard\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the field-set decision lands on a curated subset rather than\n16\t    the full CRD spec, or restricts additional backend combinations, the wizard's\n17\t    field mapping and validation rules are rewritten to the decided specification;\n18\t    the epic itself remains, with scope and form structure reworked.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: -1\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 4\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Feature Store instance create form wizard\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tBuild the guided create form wizard in the odh-dashboard frontend that lets a platform\n41\tadministrator deploy a new Feature Store instance without YAML editing or CLI access. The\n42\twizard is a PatternFly 6 form mapping to the `FeatureStore` CRD spec (feast.dev/v1),\n43\tsubmitting a valid custom resource through the dashboard's existing `/api/k8s/*`\n44\tpass-through. The implementation follows established dashboard form patterns and uses the\n45\tvalidated engineering prototype (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) as a reference, reusing\n46\twhatever is architecturally aligned.\n47\t\n48\t## Scope\n49\t\n50\t- React form wizard (PatternFly 6) covering, per the decided field-set specification:\n51\t  namespace selection, registry type, online store backend, offline store backend,\n52\t  authorization mode, and scaling parameters — including TLS settings and materialization\n53\t  scheduling where the field set requires them.\n54\t- Client-side validation of inputs against CRD schema constraints (required fields, valid\n55\t  backend combinations, scaling prerequisites) with inline guidance, derived from the CRD\n56\t  OpenAPI schema; server-side rejection errors from the K8s API surfaced in the UI.\n57\t- Submission of a valid `FeatureStore` CR via the K8s API through the existing\n58\t  `/api/k8s/*` pass-through using the admin's forwarded token.\n59\t- Feature-flag gating of the wizard consistent with the `OdhDashboardConfig` flag.\n60\t- Air-gapped support: all form options, validation rules, and assets bundled in the\n61\t  dashboard's static assets — no external network fetches.\n62\t- Write access limited to admin users (write controls not rendered for non-admins), with the\n63\t  wizard reachable only through the admin-gated route.\n64\t\n65\t## Acceptance Criteria\n66\t\n67\t- Given a platform administrator, opening the create flow shows a guided wizard rendering\n68\t  all fields required by the decided field-set specification without error, and submitting\n69\t  produces a valid `FeatureStore` CR accepted by the K8s API.\n70\t- Inline validation provides guidance for CRD schema constraints (required fields, valid\n71\t  backend combinations, scaling prerequisites) before submission.\n72\t- If the K8s API rejects a submitted CR, the validation error is surfaced in the form.\n73\t- The wizard functions with no external network access — form options, validation rules, and\n74\t  UI assets are bundled at build time.\n75\t- Non-admin users cannot reach the create flow (write controls and admin route enforcement).\n76\t- The prototype's reusable elements have been assessed and reused or consciously discarded\n77\t  with rationale.\n78\t- Form fields validated against the feast.dev/v1 CRD OpenAPI schema.\n79\t\n80\t## HLR Traceability\n81\t\n82\t- P0: deploy a new FeatureStore instance from the dashboard via a guided form wizard.\n83\t- P2: inline form validation guidance for CRD schema constraints (bundled — shares the same\n84\t  form surface and validation logic).\n85\t- P1 (shared): disconnected/air-gapped functioning of the admin UI.\n86\t\n87\tDepends on: the decided field-set and validation-constraint specification, and the UXD\n88\twireframes/interaction patterns for the wizard. The RBAC/feature-flag configuration changes\n89\trun in parallel; correct admin permissions are verified by this epic's acceptance criteria\n90\trather than a work dependency.\n91\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87a86ab7efa4cc07","agent_id":"aba39eb4d9d2cfbec","session_id":"ca7cb4a8-97e2-442a-8df6-df0a1f4664f3","uuid":"afbd511e-c48c-4b86-8981-8995a7670dae","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:18:30.638Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-824c53817a3db0ae","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
