{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b75a1b176a3ecb2a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E005\n3\ttitle: Feature Store management list, detail, and delete pages\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: -1\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Feature Store management list, detail, and delete pages\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tBuild the Feature Store management surface in the odh-dashboard frontend: a list page\n35\tshowing all `FeatureStore` instances across namespaces accessible to the user, a read-only\n36\tdetail/inspect view of any instance, admin-initiated delete with a confirmation dialog, and\n37\treal-time deployment status tracking. Non-admin (viewer) users can browse instances but see\n38\tno write controls.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Management list page: all `FeatureStore` CRs across the user's accessible namespaces, each\n43\t  row showing name, namespace, deployment status (from `.status.conditions`), and creation\n44\t  timestamp, with inspect and delete actions.\n45\t- Status tracking: list/detail status reflects real-time readiness using the dashboard's\n46\t  existing K8s watch/list patterns (no manual refresh), updating from \"Deploying\" to \"Ready\"\n47\t  as conditions are met.\n48\t- Read-only detail/inspect view: full `FeatureStore` CR spec (configured backends, registry\n49\t  type, authorization mode, scaling settings, TLS status, materialization schedule) and\n50\t  current status conditions, rendered without truncation; links to the Feast UI Route when\n51\t  available for browsing feature metadata.\n52\t- Delete flow: confirmation dialog, then `DELETE` of the `FeatureStore` CR via the existing\n53\t  `/api/k8s/*` pass-through; the feast-operator's finalizers handle cleanup of owned\n54\t  resources.\n55\t- Viewer gating: non-admin users see list and detail views but no create or delete controls\n56\t  (admin status check per existing dashboard patterns); write enforcement remains at the K8s\n57\t  API via the user's token.\n58\t- Feature-flag gating consistent with the `OdhDashboardConfig` flag.\n59\t- Air-gapped support: no external network fetches in list/detail/delete rendering.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- Given FeatureStore instances exist in namespaces the admin can access, the management page\n64\t  lists all of them with name, namespace, status, and creation timestamp, matching\n65\t  `kubectl get featurestores -A` for those namespaces.\n66\t- After instance creation, the list shows a \"Deploying\"-equivalent status that transitions\n67\t  to \"Ready\" when conditions are met, updating within the dashboard's watch/poll cycle\n68\t  without manual refresh.\n69\t- Clicking an instance shows the full CRD spec and status conditions in a read-only view,\n70\t  with all spec fields rendered without truncation.\n71\t- Delete with confirmation removes the `FeatureStore` CR via the K8s API; the instance\n72\t  disappears from the list and `kubectl get featurestore <name> -n <ns>` returns NotFound,\n73\t  with the operator cleaning up owned Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, CronJobs, HPAs,\n74\t  PDBs, and Routes.\n75\t- A non-admin (viewer) user sees list and detail views but no create or delete controls.\n76\t- Pages function without external network access.\n77\t\n78\t## HLR Traceability\n79\t\n80\t- P0: view all FeatureStore instances with name, namespace, status, creation time.\n81\t- P0: inspect the configuration of any instance in a read-only detail view.\n82\t- P0: delete a FeatureStore instance with a confirmation dialog.\n83\t- P0: deployment progress / readiness status visible in real time.\n84\t- P1 (shared): non-admin viewers browse but cannot create/delete; disconnected/air-gapped\n85\t  functioning.\n86\t\n87\tDepends on: the UXD wireframes/interaction patterns for the management page. The RBAC /\n88\tfeature-flag configuration changes run in parallel; correct viewer and admin behavior is\n89\tverified by this epic's acceptance criteria rather than a work dependency.\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87a86ab7efa4cc07","agent_id":"aba39eb4d9d2cfbec","session_id":"ca7cb4a8-97e2-442a-8df6-df0a1f4664f3","uuid":"ada561b0-92e2-4042-bebe-4970eddafc5f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:18:34.671Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b75a1b176a3ecb2a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
