ces, and identify gaps\n47\t  the dashboard form must compensate for client-side.\n48\t- Confirm the feast.dev/v1 CRD schema is stable for the RHOAI 3.5 cycle (strategy assumption\n49\t  marked \"needs validation\"); flag any anticipated breaking changes.\n50\t- Confirm admin role bindings grant `feast.dev/featurestores` write verbs with the extended\n51\t  dashboard ClusterRole.\n52\t- Assess the prototype draft PR for architectural alignment with the formal path and\n53\t  identify reusable elements.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- A validation report documents reconciliation behavior for dashboard-created CRs, delete\n58\t  cleanup, webhook validation coverage, and CRD stability findings, with pass/fail per item.\n59\t- Any gaps requiring dashboard-side compensation (client-side validation, error surfacing)\n60\t  are enumerated and communicated to the dashboard implementation.\n61\t- Prototype alignment assessment is delivered, stating what can be reused versus rebuilt.\n62\t- No feast-operator code changes are required, or any required changes are raised as\n63\t  follow-ups with impact stated.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- Risk-reduction for the P0 HLRs (deploy, view, inspect, delete, status tracking): confirms\n68\t  the operator-side assumptions those HLRs rely on. Does not itself deliver an HLR.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87a86ab7efa4cc07","agent_id":"aba39eb4d9d2cfbec","session_id":"ca7cb4a8-97e2-442a-8df6-df0a1f4664f3","uuid":"4a26691b-e31f-472c-bfae-595497ae1335","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:18:35.495Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a1fef19cf99cdfe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
