are both P0;\n39\tE008 (docs-authoring) is exempt and correctly derives P1 from the strategy's `priority: Major`.\n40\tNo triage (full decomposition), so multi-epic output is expected.\n41\t\n42\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n43\tCross-checked all 13 diagram edges against epic frontmatter `dependencies` — exact match in\n44\tboth directions (E004: [E001, E002]; E005: [E002]; E007: [E003, E004, E005, E006];\n45\tE008: [E002–E007]; E001/E002/E003/E006: []), with arrows drawn dependency → dependent per\n46\tconvention. No cycles, no invalid edges, no branch files (none needed — the E001 outcome space\n47\tis a continuum, correctly handled via `gate_failure_impact` instead of conditional branches).\n48\tNo konflux-onboarding, repo-onboarding, or license-validation epics exist, so rules 7/8/10\n49\tparallelism constraints are not applicable. Parallel-eligible work is correctly not serialized:\n50\tE003 (RBAC/manifests) runs parallel to E004/E005 (React frontend) with the feature-flag and\n51\tpermission coupling correctly handled as acceptance-criteria gates rather than a DAG edge\n52\t(configuration reference, per Rule 13/15); E006 runs parallel to E004 by Rule 13 exclusion.\n53\tRule 11 edges (E002–E007 → E008) are valid and correctly do not trigger priority inheritance.\n54\tCritical path length 4 (E001/E002 → E004 → E007 → E008) matches the M-standard heuristic (3–4)\n55\tand the summary's declared `critical_path_length: 4`. One minor observation: E006's\n56\t\"client-side compensation gaps\" deliverable is an input to E004's form validation with no DAG\n57\trelation — acceptably handled as an AC-gated risk-reduction input, but the parallel scheduling\n58\tmeans the communication path relies on team coordination rather than any pipeline structure.\n59\t\n60\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n61\tEvery epic carries a single component/team tuple, and all component names are canonical per\n62\t`.context/rhai-components.txt` (AI Core Dashboard, Feature Store, UXD, QE, Documentation —\n63\tall verified present). No epic bundles multiple teams. Work-product types are correctly\n64\tseparated: UXD design authoring (E002), code implementation (E003–E005), validation reporting\n65\t(E006), QE testing (E007), and documentation (E008) are distinct epics. No scope duplication\n66\tacross siblings: E004 (wizard) and E005 (management pages) build distinct UI surfaces; E006\n67\t(operator validation) and E007 (UI functional validation) are different teams, components, and\n68\tscopes; the shared mentions (feature flag, admin status check) are incidental config overlap,\n69\tnot duplicated work products. One minor observation: E005 bundles four P0 HLRs (list, detail,\n70\tdelete, status tracking) plus viewer gating into a single epic — defensible as one logical\n71\tmanagement surface sharing one data model and built against an existing prototype, but it is\n72\tthe largest epic in the set and worth monitoring for sprint overrun.\n73\t\n74\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n75\tE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome (curated field set vs. full CRD exposure,\n76\tbackend-combination restrictions) rewrites E004's scope, and it has a downstream dependent\n77\t(E004) with `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-8007-E001` correctly set, `gate_failure_impact` populated\n78\twith both `action: rewrite` and a concrete `fallback_approach`, and the `gated_by` target\n79\tpresent in E004's direct `dependencies` list. E002 is correctly typed Implementation (design\n80\tartifact production, not uncertainty resolution — the UXD timeline question changes\n81\tscheduling, not structure, and the decomposition says exactly that). E006 is correctly typed\n82\tImplementation: it verifies already-documented operator behavior and produces a concrete\n83\tvalidation-report artifact; the assumptions it checks are marked \"confirmed\" in the strategy.\n84\tNo epic lists an Investigation in `dependencies` without `gated_by` (only E004 depends on\n85\tE001, and it is gated). No other `gated_by` fields are set, so no scheduling dependencies are\n86\tmisclassified as gates.\n87\t\n88\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n89\tSignal fields are type-appropriate everywhere: E001 (Investigation) carries\n90\t`investigation_signals`; E002–E008 (Implementation) carry `ai_signals`; no cross-contamination.\n91\tAll frontmatter signal values match the rationale tables in the corresponding ai-signals files\n92\t(checked all 8, one-to-one). Rationales are justified against strategy content: E003's\n93\t`change_specificity: 1` (exact file, verbs, resource), E004's `open_questions: -1` and\n94\t`human_process_gates: -1` (field-curation gate, UXD sign-off), E001's\n95\t`human_judgment_required: -2` (PM field-set decision), and the `architecture_claims: 1` values\n96\tfor E003/E004/E005/E006 are substantiated — odh-dashboard.md, feast.md, and PLATFORM.md all\n97\texist in `.context/architecture-context/`. Score arithmetic not checked (pipeline-computed).\n98\tOne borderline value: E002's `open_questions: 0` — the E001 field-set decision could reshape\n99\tthe wizard wireframes, though the interaction-pattern work proceeds against the strategy's\n100\tfixed field groups; the rationale is coherent, so this is at most an arguable call.\n101\t\n102\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n103\tEvery epic has testable, strategy-derived ACs (list matches `kubectl get featurestores -A`,\n104\twatch-cycle status transition, viewer token refused at K8s API, air-gapped deployment on a\n105\tdisconnected cluster, sign-offs recorded). Rule-mandated ACs are present where applicable:\n106\tfeature-flag/rollback gating (E003 flag default off; E004/E005 flag-gated pages; E007\n107\tregression check that clusters without Feast see no UI changes), docs technical review with\n108\trecorded sign-off (E008), and no konflux-chain epics exist so the build-pipeline AC is not\n109\tapplicable. No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID — grep across all 8 epic bodies\n110\tfound